{"files": {"SKILL.md": "## Core Rules\n\n- Gather context first: review docs, task details, and prior artifacts before acting.\n- Implement exactly what was requested; do not reinterpret or expand scope.\n- Keep edits narrow and protect behavior that is already correct.\n- Before introducing a new pattern, check and learn from similar working code.\n- Use available validation to confirm outcomes before declaring done.\n- Act with strict expected outcomes, test to confirm those expectations, and fix immediately when results differ.\n- Communicate in short, clear statements.\n\n## Tool Discipline\n\n- Use one chained terminal invocation for dependent steps when possible.\n- Read the entire target file before making changes.\n\n## Execution Flow\n\n- Start with the explicit requested change.\n- Ship the smallest complete fix that satisfies the ask.\n- Re-validate the touched target after each meaningful edit.\n- If there is a persistent notes area, leave a brief generalized takeaway.\n"}, "schema_version": 1}